I have misplace the address to mail bugs off to for nethack
so if someone can make sute the development team gets the
following:
 
There is a error in the Xenix 386 compiler version 2.3.0 (and
presumably any other 386 version of the xenix compiler).
in rnd the parameter passed in is declared a register value
in the functions cpp subsitutes for RND(x) rand(x) % ...
this causes the compiler to generate the following assembly
instruction idiv esi, this an invalid instruction on the
386.  to get around this one use remove the register declaration
from the incoming parameter.  
 
I suggest that the  develpmente team put some kind of conditional
compilation in the code to circumvent this.


